# Derived by hand from Semantics Appendix B (`!MergeAll` fires the values of the inputs that fired, in the list's order): a click on `a` fires the first and third inputs, one on `b` the second.
test the_list_merges_in_its_order

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="a")
    1: Ui.Button(label="b")
    2: Ui.Label(text="none")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="1,3")

tick 2
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
